# .clinerules — granary (tej/granary)

## Project

granary is a pure-OCaml SQL engine — a concept port of SQLite targeting MirageOS
unikernels. No C stubs, fresh on-disk format, single-writer/multi-reader MVCC with
snapshot isolation. OCaml 5.4. Pre-release (0.0.1). **Entirely AI-authored**
(disclosure level: `ai-generated`). See `README.md` and `ROADMAP.md`.

---

## 1. Worktree discipline — ALWAYS

**The repo root (`/home/tej/projects/granary`) stays on `main` at all times.**
Never commit directly to `main`. Never work in the repo root.

For every task:

1. Create a feature branch and worktree **before touching any code**:
   ```
   git worktree add ../granary-<slug> -b feat/<slug>
   ```
   All file edits and command execution happen inside `../granary-<slug>/`.

2. When work is complete and tests are green, open a PR (see §5 Forgejo CLI).

3. After the PR is merged, clean up:
   ```
   git worktree remove ../granary-<slug>
   git branch -d feat/<slug>
   ```

Slug is a short kebab-case description of the task.

---

## 2. Subagent orchestration — ALWAYS

Break every non-trivial task into independent subtasks and delegate each via
`new_task`. Do not do multi-step work in a single agent context.

**Orchestrator loop:**

1. **Decompose** — identify independent units (failing test, implementation,
   formatting fix, lint fix). List them explicitly.
2. **Delegate** — spawn a `new_task` for each. Each brief must be self-contained:
   include the worktree path, files to touch, acceptance criterion, and context.
3. **Review** — when a subtask returns, critically verify the diff:
   - Did it follow TDD (failing test first, minimum production code)?
   - Does `dune runtest` pass inside the container?
   - Does formatting pass (`dune build @fmt`)?
   - Does lint pass (merlint, zero findings)?
   - Any unintended changes to other files?
4. **Reject or accept** — fix or re-delegate if review fails. Never silently accept.
5. **Integrate** — once all subtasks pass review, assemble the PR.

---

## 3. Strict TDD — non-negotiable

Every change follows **red → green → refactor**:

1. **Red** — write a failing test. Run it. Confirm it fails *for the right reason*.
2. **Green** — write the minimum production code to make it pass. Nothing more.
3. **Refactor** — clean up with the suite green.

Rules:
- No production code without a failing test that demands it.
- One behavior per test. Tests are the specification.
- Never weaken, skip, or delete a test to make the suite pass.
- Tests use **alcotest** (unit/integration) and **qcheck-alcotest** (property).
  Prefer property tests for invariants.
- `dune runtest` must be green before every commit.

---

## 4. Build / test / lint / format

All dune commands run inside the **`granary-dev`** Podman image. Never run dune
directly on the host. From inside the worktree directory:

```sh
# Build
podman run --rm -v "$(pwd)":/workspace:Z -w /workspace granary-dev \
  opam exec -- dune build

# Test
podman run --rm -v "$(pwd)":/workspace:Z -w /workspace granary-dev \
  opam exec -- dune runtest

# Format check (ocamlformat 0.29.0, janestreet profile)
podman run --rm -v "$(pwd)":/workspace:Z -w /workspace granary-dev \
  opam exec -- dune build @fmt

# Apply formatting
podman run --rm -v "$(pwd)":/workspace:Z -w /workspace granary-dev \
  opam exec -- dune fmt

# Lint (merlint — must be zero findings)
podman run --rm -v "$(pwd)":/workspace:Z -w /workspace granary-dev \
  merlint --color=never

# Coverage (threshold 85%)
./scripts/coverage.sh
```

If the `granary-dev` image isn't built yet:
```sh
podman build -t granary-dev .
```

---

## 5. Forgejo CLI — correct usage

**CLI selection:** This repo is on `git.iotready.com` — use `forgejo`. For repos on `github.com`, use `gh` instead.

**PR analysis:** Post as **comments** (`forgejo issue comment`), not formal reviews — the coder and reviewer are the same user. Do not use the Forgejo review API.

The `forgejo` CLI (`~/.local/bin/forgejo`) is authenticated against
**https://git.iotready.com** as **tej (admin)**. Repo: `tej/granary`.

**Critical gotcha:** `forgejo issue label …` and label/milestone subcommands
**misroute to an org endpoint** and return `API error (404): GetOrgByName` for
user-owned repos like `tej/*`. Never use those subcommands. Use the generic API
passthrough:

```bash
# List labels
forgejo api GET /repos/tej/granary/labels

# Create label
forgejo api POST /repos/tej/granary/labels \
  -f name="type:bug" -f color="#d73a4a" -f description="..."

# Create milestone
forgejo api POST /repos/tej/granary/milestones \
  -f title="M02" -f description="..."

# Create issue (with milestone id + label ids — use --input for arrays/ints)
echo '{"title":"...","body":"...","milestone":3,"labels":[1,4]}' \
  | forgejo api POST /repos/tej/granary/issues --input -

# Read/list issues (native subcommands work fine)
forgejo issue view tej/granary <n>
forgejo issue list tej/granary

# Open PR
echo '{"title":"feat: ...","body":"...","head":"feat/<slug>","base":"main"}' \
  | forgejo api POST /repos/tej/granary/pulls --input -
```

The REST API requires the CLI/token — plain `curl` returns 403 (private repo).

---

## 6. Conventions

- `lib/` must remain Mirage-compatible: no `Unix`, `Lwt_unix`, `threads`, or
  `*-unix` library deps. Unix backends live in `bin/` and test harnesses only.
- Small, single-purpose modules with `.mli` interfaces.
- `Printf`/`Format` over `Fmt`. Descriptive identifiers.
- Flat, behavior-oriented test suite under `test/`.
- ocamlformat 0.29.0 (janestreet profile) — the `.ocamlformat` `version` field
  must match exactly.
- No comments explaining *what* code does. Only add one when the *why* is
  non-obvious.

---

## 7. Issues & deferred work

File deferred or discovered work as a Forgejo issue **immediately**. Never bury
it in a code comment or `TODO`. Use `forgejo api POST /repos/tej/granary/issues`
with the right labels and milestone, then reference it (`#NNN`) where relevant.
